<title>USA: Circuit Systems to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Circuit Systems to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>ELK GROVE VILLAGE, Ill. 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Circuit Systems Inc said Friday its board authorized the repurchase, from time to time, of up to 250,000 shares of common stock at the market price.</p>
<p>Circuit Systems said its board believes the stock is undervalued and the repurchase at favorable prices would be in the best interests of shareholders.</p>
<p>The company has about 5.3 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Circuit System shares were unchanged at 4-5/8.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
